WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:04.350
The Schrodinger Equation is the key equation
in quantum physics that explains how particles

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.180
in quantum physics behave.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.650
You wanna know where your electron is going
to go?

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:10.660
That’s the Shrodinger equation you’ll
need.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.640
So why does it look so complicated?

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:16.230
Well it’s because in quantum physics, when
you are describing what a thing like an electron

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:21.481
will do, it doesn’t follow the rules of
particles it follows the rules of waves, and

00:00:21.481 --> 00:00:25.029
that’s what these psi’s are, they are
wavefunctions.

00:00:25.029 --> 00:00:29.880
Okay so an electron is a wave, and a wave
can evolve in space and in time, but it can’t

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:34.550
evolve in any old way, there are constraints
about how it can evolve, and those constraints?

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:37.690
That’s what the Shrodinger equation is telling
us.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:42.030
It says that over time (that’s this bit)
the total energy has to stay the same.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:46.309
And this total energy is made of the kinetic
energy (that’s this bit), and potential

00:00:46.309 --> 00:00:47.699
energy (that’s this bit).

00:00:47.699 --> 00:00:51.879
An example of a potential energy for an electron
is just being in an atom.

00:00:51.879 --> 00:00:55.960
So if you want to see what a quantum object
will do in the future, you need to find the

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:59.840
wavefunction that will satisfy all these bits
of the Shrodinger equation.

